    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d144">

                <pb facs="0331" n="269" xml:id="pg269"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.CC/4–1145</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Soviet Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gromyko</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-04-11">April 11, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to bring to your
                    attention that when the question on the organization of the work of the Jurists’
                    Committee was under consideration the Soviet Government set forth a proposal to
                    elect four chairmen from representatives of the four nations<anchor n="27"
                        xml:id="d144-f1"/> in whose name invitations to the Conference and to the
                    meetings of the Jurists’ Committee were sent out.<anchor n="28" xml:id="d144-f2"
                    /> The proposal of the Soviet Government was based on the principle of equality
                    of position of the four nations. This proposal, however, was not
                        accepted.<anchor n="29" xml:id="d144-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>The Soviet Government considers such a decision wrong and expresses its
                    disagreement with the decision as it violates the principal of equality of
                    position of the four nations, in whose name invitations to the Conference were
                    sent out to other governments.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. Gromyko</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d144-f1" n="27" xml:id="d144-f1-content">
                <p>See memorandum of conversation, by Mr. Leo Pasvolsky, April 9, <ref
                        target="#pg214">p. 214</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d144-f2" n="28" xml:id="d144-f2-content">
                <p>For text of invitation to the conference of the United Nations at San Francisco,
                    see telegram 1409, February 23, midnight, to London, <ref target="#pg89">p.
                        89</ref>; for text of invitation to the meeting of the United Nations
                    Committee of Jurists at Washington, see circular telegram of March 24, midnight,
                        <ref target="#pg154">p. 154</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d144-f3" n="29" xml:id="d144-f3-content">
                <p>Jurist 11, G/8, April 9, revised as Jurist 36(11), G/26, April 13, UNCIO
                    Documents, vol. 14, pp. 42 and 52.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
